==English==

===Etymology===
Past participle of {{m|en|serrate}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|eɪtɪd|s=3}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Notched or cut like a [[saw]].
#: {{ux|en|That knife has a '''serrated''' blade.}}
# Having a row of [[sharp]] or [[tooth]]-like [[projection]]s.
#: {{ux|en|Maple leaves have '''serrated''' edges.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|notched}} {{l|en|jagged}}, {{l|en|serrate}}; see also [[Thesaurus:notched]]

